    { math: '1 · Perception is inference', note: 'The retina delivers a 2-D, upside-down, sparse signal; the brain infers the 3-D world from it. Helmholtz called it "unconscious inference" — the best-guess construction behind every perception.' },
    { math: '2 · Ambiguity proves the construction', note: 'The Necker cube flips between two interpretations with identical input; ambiguous figures show the brain choosing among hypotheses. The choice, not the image, is the experience.' },
